Downstream modifications (this repository)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository is a downstream distribution of `sorryhyun/anima_lora`
(MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Seunghyun Ji). The upstream `LICENSE`, `NOTICE` and
`LICENSE-APACHE` are kept verbatim; the modifications below are the downstream
project's own and are covered by the same MIT license.

  1. Chinese display overlay for the PySide6 GUI
     (`gui/i18n/cn_overlay.json`, `gui/i18n/overlay.py`, and the call sites listed
     in `downstream/owned-paths.txt`): TOML keys, `_GROUPS` titles and
     `presets.toml` labels are rendered in Chinese when the GUI language is
     `cn`. English/Korean/Japanese rendering is unchanged.
  2. Three i18n keys upstream was missing (`refresh`, `method`, `path_scope`) in
     `gui/i18n/{en,ko,ja,cn}.py`, plus two Chinese field-help entries in
     `gui/explanations/guides/cn/_fields.json`.
  3. Upstream-tracking tooling: `.github/workflows/upstream-sync.yml`,
     `scripts/downstream/upstream-sync.ps1`, `.downstream/*` and
     `tests/test_downstream_guards.py`.
  4. Placeholders for a planned Krea-2 line (`library/krea2/`, `scripts/krea2/`,
     `configs/krea2/`, `downstream/krea2-line-plan.md`). No Krea-2 code is
     included yet.

Planned Krea-2 work derives from https://github.com/scvxzf1/krea2-webui (MIT,
confirmed by its author) — the Krea-2 model family, NF4 self-contained
checkpoint loading, family-aware LoRA targets and the Qwen3-VL text path live
there. When that code is ported in, this section must name every ported file.

Ported as of 2026-10-18 (vendored **as-is** from krea2-webui; sha256-identical
to the source build, one marked downstream shim in `dit.py` noted below):

    library/models/krea2_raw/{__init__,attention_backend,dit,family,
      inference_runner,lora_targets,quantize,sampling,strategy,
      training_preview,uncond,weights}.py        (4200 lines total)
    scripts/krea2/probe_port.py                  (downstream probe, not ported)

Downstream shim inside the vendored `dit.py::enable_block_swap`: krea2-webui's
`ModelOffloader` is a superset of upstream's, so the extra kwargs
(`profile_jsonl` / `transfer_dtype` / `restore_mode`) are filtered by signature
instead of passed blindly. The Krea-2 block-swap path additionally needs that
superset's semantics — tracked in `downstream/krea2-line-plan.md`.

⚠ The Krea-2 *architecture* code in krea2-webui is a port of
https://github.com/krea-ai/krea-2, whose repository carries **no LICENSE file**
(checked 2026-10-18) and whose README only states the *model weights*' community
license. Resolve the code license before redistributing any such file.


